@@ -869,11 +869,11 @@
     },
     "voices": {
       "_how": "The one-shot takes' players (the game's audio components), pooled: made once and reused for take after take, not one spawned and destroyed for every take, and a cut take's fade kept with its voice, not a timer for each (the production study of 22 Nov, section 5, item 9: 0.4 to 1.2 ms a frame at 235 s). warm are made before the battle; more are made as needed up to most; with every one sounding, the take nearest its end gives way. pool false (or the game's -TheaterLandVoicesSpawned) spawns one for each take, as before.",
-      "pool": false,
-      "_pool": "false until the 3D pre-check and a Mac sound-on run pass (handoff 22 Nov 17:30Z): the scene code is written but has not been compiled against Unreal.",
